{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:13.20.570","page_type":"section"},"citation":"13.20.570","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.570","content_hash":"ed628eefcf902cc82da0f40561952d28ee2707829ba4bf70820df1f377284297","heading":"Liquid waste hauler discharge permit application, application fee.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.20.570:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.570","text":"(a) Applications for a liquid waste hauler discharge permit shall be made to the WPCD and shall contain the following information:\n(1) Name and address, including business address of liquid waste hauler.\n(2) Quantity, capacity, license plate number, and type of all vehicles operated by hauler for the purpose of hauling liquid waste.\n(3) Types of materials pumped by hauler including a waste characterization profile on each type of material.\n(4) Proof of insurance in the following types and amounts:\n(i) Bodily injury, nonvehicular: $300,000 each occurrence.\n(ii) Property damage, nonvehicular: $100,000 each occurrence.\n(iii) Automobile insurance: $100,000 single occurrence, $300,000 aggregate, $50,000 property damage.\n(5) Any other information deemed necessary by the Utilities Director in order to review the application.\n(b) An application must be accompanied by the appropriate fee before it will be considered by the Utilities Director. Permit application fees shall be set forth in a fee schedule promulgated by the Utilities Director and approved by the City Manager.\n(c) The Utilities Director may issue a permit if, after review of the application, the Utilities Director finds:\n(1) The liquid waste is domestic generated waste or commercial/food waste with the exception of grease trap waste; and\n(2) The liquid waste may be discharged into the WPCD disposal facility without causing pass-through or interference; and\n(3) The liquid waste meets all applicable Federal, State, and City requirements. Any permit issued shall be valid for a period of one year following issuance. (Ord. 20157 § 2, 12-4-18.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"03f8f40e-d22a-57cf-bafa-7ce0487821fb"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.20.570","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.570","content_hash":"2ec354208fbeae1e444aec71b6c26d54811b771f9a6a1229f85ee6cdd7cddacc","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.20.570:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.20.570:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.570","text":"(a) Applications for a liquid waste hauler discharge permit shall be made to the WPCD and shall contain the following information:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"042feb58-c151-5ea0-a6bf-ad71d8474e19"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.20.570","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.570","content_hash":"74d7ef08cb3906bfe1c29ebef97ab2aba86b501b82dbcc2ffae51dfa3f6d23a0","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.20.570:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.20.570:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.570","text":"(1) Name and address, including business address of liquid waste hauler.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"a14ede8a-644d-52e8-8e67-610cba6c5fc7"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.20.570","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.570","content_hash":"0f8151b74acc327fffed71f10c10672e2a3ffeeef3bd552604b3da335e8